===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[formal]] [[investigation]], often held before a [[jury]], especially one into the [[cause]] of a [[death]]
#* {{RQ:Bindloss Dust of Conflict|chapter=4|passage=The '''inquest''' on keeper Davidson was duly held, and at the commencement seemed likely to cause Tony Palliser less anxiety than he had expected.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 August 25|author=Christian Wolmar|title=Croydon tram crash: the questions haven't been answered|journal=RAIL|issue=938|page=58|text=However, the 'accidental death' verdict of the jury in the '''inquest''' into the Croydon tram accident of November 2016 is the latest episode in a saga that seems likely to prevent the full story of this eminently preventable disaster from ever being exposed.}}
# An [[inquiry]], typically into an undesired outcome
# The jury hearing such an [[inquiry]], and the result of the inquiry
# {{lb|en|rare|obsolete}} [[enquiry]]; [[quest]]; [[search]]
#* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=the laborious and vexatious '''inquest''' that the soul must make after science}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|6|11|passage=Hauing of late by diligent '''inquest''', <br>Prouided him a sword of meanest sort}}

